      "content": "Thanks for the draft. It's a good start, but I actually think we need to pull back on the explicit numbers. \n\nEven mentioning \"8% movement\" in the very first paragraph might be a mistake. Given how sensitive these clients are, if they see that specific figure, they're going to fixate on it and start asking questions that we aren't ready to answer yet.\n\nCan we do a second version where we remove the 8% entirely? Instead of calling it a \"movement,\" let's characterize this period as a \"strategic period of consolidation\" or \"portfolio recalibration.\" I want the summary to focus on the strength of our position so they don't even feel the need to ask about a specific percentage drop. We need to steer the conversation toward the long-term outlook immediately.",
